<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ayudha dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">770 CE – 816 CE (approx.) · capital Kannauj</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived dynasty of Kannauj whose kings became pawns in the struggle between the Palas, Pratiharas and Rashtrakutas.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ayudhas held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> in the late 8th century after the decline of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/varman-dynasty-of-kannauj">Varman dynasty of Kannauj</a>. The dynasty is known only from references in the inscriptions of neighbouring powers and in Jain literature, and its first known king is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indrayudha">Indrayudha</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> was the symbolic capital of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and control of it was the prize in the tripartite struggle. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dharmapala-pala-emperor">Dharmapala</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/pala-empire">Pala Empire</a> deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indrayudha">Indrayudha</a> and placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chakrayudha">Chakrayudha</a> on the throne, holding a great court where northern kings acknowledged the new ruler. Chakrayudha was effectively a Pala client.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 816 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagabhata-ii">Nagabhata II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gurjara-pratihara">Gurjara-Pratihara</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chakrayudha">Chakrayudha</a> and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>, which became the Pratihara capital. Nothing is known of the Ayudhas afterwards.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 770 CE – 816 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:75.02%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>770 CE – 816 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kannauj</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Indrayudha, Chakrayudha</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ayudhas of Kannauj</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=793&amp;focus=ayudha-dynasty" aria-label="Ayudha dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6783 1186 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ayudha dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7103 1442L7103 1442M7103 1442L7253 1492M7103 1442L7103 1442"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7103 1442h0M7253 1492h0M7103 1442h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7103 1442h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7103 1442h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kannauj. <a href="/atlas?year=793&amp;focus=ayudha-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
